course: dictionary
lesson: 10975
title: Who is the warden?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A warden is a person whose job is to look after a place or the people in it. Context tells you which kind of warden is meant. «Deacons, elders, church wardens and many volunteers care for people, buildings and money.» The clues are people, buildings and money, so a church warden looks after things that matter to a church.
explain: «A found dog should not be grabbed, because a scared dog may bite; a grown-up can call the dog warden or take it to a vet.» The clues are found dog, bite and vet, so a dog warden is a person who deals with dogs that have been found. Read the words around the word, and they tell you the job.
explain: The same word can mean different jobs. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense. If the place is a park, a warden looks after the park. If it is a car, a traffic warden checks the parking.
fact: A warden is a person whose job is to look after a place or the people in it.
fact: In the US, a prison governor is called a warden.
fact: A traffic warden (UK) checks that cars are parked legally.
fact: A churchwarden helps run a parish, which is a church and its community.
fact: Context clues, such as the place or the job in the sentence, show you which kind of warden is meant.
exercise: «Deacons, elders, church wardens and many volunteers care for people, buildings and money.» What do church wardens care for, according to the sentence? | *People, buildings and money | Cars parked outside | The church bells only | Dogs and cats
exercise: What is the job of a traffic warden (UK)? | *Checks that cars are parked legally | Plays the organ in church | Looks after dogs that have been found | Runs a prison in the US
exercise: «A found dog should not be grabbed, because a scared dog may bite.» Why should you not grab a found dog? | *It may be scared and bite | It will always run away | It is too small to hold | It belongs to a warden
test: In the US, what does warden mean? | A park gate | *A prison governor | A bus driver | A kind of bird
test: A park warden's job is to... | *Look after the park and the people in it | Teach swimming in the lake | Check the cars parked on the road | Sell ice cream in the park
exam: What does a churchwarden help to run? | A parrot | A railway | *A parish | A zoo
